The Three Stages of Verification:
1. Software Waveform Simulation (GTKWave)
Before loading the core onto physical hardware, we run our testbench using Icarus Verilog (iverilog). It creates a trace file (.vcd) that lets us inspect every wire across time:
 * Check 1: Does the Program Counter (pc) increment by 4 on every cycle (0x0, 0x4, 0x8)?
 * Check 2: Does the wb_result bus show the expected math results?
 * Check 3: Does branch_taken pulse high for one clock cycle and flush Barrier 1?
2. The UART Serial Console Test
We connect the core to a serial transmitter wire (UART) linked to your computer via USB.
We compile an assembly program that runs both a standard software PopCount loop and our single-cycle Cheat-Code instruction. The core prints its execution profile straight to your terminal:
